# Shared non-region defaults (timeouts, TLS paths). Prefer region files for DATA_DIR / LISTEN / probes.
# Local: ./scripts/start_server.sh pacific|caribbean  (sources .env.{region} when present)
# Prod:  systemd ipv6-web@pacific with EnvironmentFile=.env.%i — see docs/development.md

PROJECT_ROOT=.

# REGION and DATA_DIR belong in .env.pacific / .env.caribbean (or start scripts / systemd).
# REGION=pacific
# DATA_DIR=./data/pacific

# When the collector runs as root, set this so JSON under DATA_DIR is chowned for the web server user (optional group).
# COLLECTOR_DATA_USER=franck
# COLLECTOR_DATA_GROUP=franck

# Web (HTTPS only — requires certs; see certs/README.md)
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL — set per region in .env.{region}
# LISTEN — set per region (pacific :8082, caribbean :8083)

TLS_CERT_FILE=certs/cert.pem
TLS_KEY_FILE=certs/key.pem

# Monthly 6/6 IPv4 drill (main site only; UTC day 6). See docs/development.md.
# IPV4_OUTAGE_SKIP=1
# IPV4_OUTAGE_FORCE=1
# IPV4_OUTAGE_HOST= — set per region

# PROBE_* and HEALTHZ_CORS_* — set per region in .env.{region}.example

# Skip Hurricane Electric bgp.he.net country scrape (keep last snapshot in JSON).
# COLLECTOR_SKIP_HE_BGP=1

# Daemon: one economy per interval (production often 4h; dev default in code is 10m).
# COLLECTOR_PER_COUNTRY_INTERVAL=4h

# RPKI via RIPEstat (stat.ripe.net). Register app with stat@ripe.net if volume grows.
# COLLECTOR_SKIP_RPKI=1
# COLLECTOR_RPKI_MAX_PREFIXES_PER_ASN=10
# COLLECTOR_RPKI_REFRESH_INTERVAL=168h
# COLLECTOR_RPKI_MIN_INTERVAL=300ms
# RIPESTAT_SOURCEAPP — set per region (pacific-ipv6-monitor / caribbean-ipv6-monitor)

# Timeouts
DNS_TIMEOUT=5s
HTTP_CLIENT_TIMEOUT=15s
SMTP_TIMEOUT=10s
CHECK_DOMAIN_DEADLINE=120s
